## 5. Building with AI (techniques)

| Concept | One-line definition |
|---|---|
| **Prompt engineering** | The craft of designing and optimising prompts to steer LLMs toward the desired output by supplying context, instructions, and examples. Techniques: zero-shot, one/few/multi-shot, chain-of-thought (CoT), zero-shot CoT. `/discover/what-is-prompt-engineering` |
| **Context engineering** | Systematically assembling the right information, tools, and memory into a model's context window so it can respond accurately, going beyond single-prompt wording. `/discover/ai-context-engineering` |
| **Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG)** | A framework that combines information retrieval (search/databases) with an LLM so answers are grounded in your data: retrieve and pre-process, then generate with that context. Improves freshness and factual accuracy, reducing hallucinations. `/use-cases/retrieval-augmented-generation` |
| **Fine-tuning** | Further training a pre-trained model on a task-specific dataset (transfer learning) to specialise it. Alters model parameters (vs RAG, which augments prompts). Methods include supervised fine-tuning and LoRA. `/use-cases/fine-tuning-ai-models` |
| **Generative UI (GenUI)** | Interfaces an LLM builds in real time rather than from static templates, adapting layout and components to user intent. Spectrum: static (fixed library), declarative (structured schema), open-ended (raw HTML/CSS). `/discover/generative-ui` |
| **AI inference** | The "doing" stage: a trained model takes new data and produces output (prediction, image, decision). Life cycle: training, fine-tuning, inference, serving. Where AI delivers business value. `/discover/what-is-ai-inference` |
| **Batch inference** | Running model predictions over a large, fixed set of data all at once (offline), as opposed to real-time per-request inference. `/discover/what-is-batch-inference` |
| **Inference optimization** | Techniques (quantisation, batching, caching, hardware acceleration) to make model serving faster, cheaper, and more efficient at scale. `/discover/inference-optimization` |

