## 6. Applied AI: language, vision, speech

| Concept | One-line definition |
|---|---|
| **Natural language processing (NLP)** | A branch of AI that uses ML to reveal the structure and meaning of text and to act on it. Covers recognition, generation, and understanding (NLU). Used for sentiment, classification, document analysis. `/learn/what-is-natural-language-processing` |
| **Entity extraction** | An NLP technique that identifies and classifies named entities (people, places, organisations, dates, amounts) within unstructured text. `/discover/what-is-entity-extraction` |
| **Computer vision** | A field of AI that interprets and analyses visual data (images, video) to derive meaning: object detection, classification, OCR, face/landmark detection. (Product page; related concept page is CNNs.) `/vision` |
| **Speech recognition (Speech-to-Text)** | Converts spoken language into written text using AI/ML; supports 125+ languages with synchronous, asynchronous, and streaming modes, powered by the Chirp foundation model. (Product page.) `/speech-to-text` |
| **Recommendation systems** | The ML technology behind content discovery and "you may also like" suggestions, surfacing relevant items at the right time. Approaches: Recommendations AI, BigQuery ML matrix factorisation, Vertex AI matching (ScaNN). (Use-case page.) `/use-cases/recommendations` |

