## 7. Search & data for AI

| Concept | One-line definition |
|---|---|
| **Vector database** | A database that stores, indexes, and queries vector embeddings (numeric representations of unstructured data) for meaning-based retrieval via nearest-neighbour search (KNN/ANN). Critical for generative AI and RAG. `/discover/what-is-a-vector-database` |
| **pgvector** | An open-source PostgreSQL extension that adds vector storage and similarity search to Postgres, enabling embeddings-based queries inside a familiar database. `/discover/what-is-pgvector` |
| **Semantic search** | Search that matches on meaning and intent (using embeddings) rather than exact keywords, returning conceptually relevant results. `/discover/what-is-semantic-search` |
| **Full-text search** | Search that scans the complete text of documents to match query terms, typically with indexing for speed across large text collections. `/discover/what-is-full-text-search` |
| **Fuzzy search** | Matching that tolerates typos, misspellings, and approximate strings, returning near-matches rather than only exact ones. `/discover/what-is-fuzzy-search` |
| **Stemming** | Reducing words to their root form (e.g. "running" to "run") so search and NLP treat variants as the same term. `/discover/what-is-stemming` |
| **Graph database** | A database that stores data as nodes and relationships (edges), optimised for traversing connections; useful for knowledge graphs that give AI business context. `/discover/what-is-a-graph-database` |

