## 9. Enterprise & process automation

| Concept | One-line definition |
|---|---|
| **Enterprise AI** | Adopting and integrating AI across an organisation at scale, with the governance, data, and infrastructure to deliver business value reliably. `/discover/what-is-enterprise-ai` |
| **AI applications** | The practical uses of AI across functions and industries (the "what AI is used for" overview). `/discover/ai-applications` |
| **Robotic process automation (RPA)** | Software "bots" that automate repetitive, rule-based digital tasks; when combined with AI it becomes intelligent automation. `/discover/what-is-robotic-process-automation` |
| **Process mining** | Analysing event-log data from business systems to discover, monitor, and improve how processes actually run. `/discover/what-is-process-mining` |
| **AI in banking / Finance AI** | Industry views of AI applied to financial services: fraud detection, risk, personalisation, and operations. `/discover/ai-in-banking`, `/discover/finance-ai` |
| **Responsible AI** | Building AI ethically and accountably: anchored in Google's AI Principles, with evaluations, review bodies, and transparency tools (Explainable AI, Model Cards). (Principles page.) `/responsible-ai` |

